  "schematicNotes": [
    {
      "id": "n_intro",
      "text": "ENGINE ROOM HARNESS C. No factory engine-bay wire or connector is reused (Dan, 2026-10-10, binding): J/B No.2, R/B No.2-5, F11 and the engine-room main wire are removed from the car. Every bay load is new wire from the glove-box fuse box (ST185-CabinPower) straight to its device plug (OEM device plug, or DT where Dan chose DT). Cabin landings (IE1 / J/B1 cowl side, the old R/B2 and R/B4 outputs, the blower) splice into factory cabin leads - cabin reuse is unchanged. Owner text: docs/electrical/ENGINE-ROOM-POWER-REDISTRIBUTION.md.",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3210,
        "y": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_split",
      "text": "ROUTE: docs/harness/routes/ROUTE-2-HARNESS-C.html (approved, rev 9). Glove box -> right kick (blower) -> under the dash -> left kick (IE1 / J/B1 / old R/B2 landings); glove box -> RH fender grommet -> RH inner fender (A/C, EPS pump) -> fan branch -> across the front: RH corner (H2), horn branch (DT 2-way per horn), LH corner (H1). Heavy DC is ST185-HeavyDC (breaks H1/H2/H3/H6a). Front lighting, retract motors and wipers drawn 2026-10-13 (Route 2 rev 10): no side marker lights on the car (Dan); F7 / F8 turn + clearance (J/B1 1H-4 / 1H-8 turn, 1H-6 TAIL), H1 / H2 high / low returns to IE1-11 / IE1-18, retract motors R2 / R3 from the OEM R8 via IE1-7/8/9/14/15/16, front wiper F9 (J/B1 1H-5 WIPER 20A + IE1-6/13/20; park switch in the motor, no relay of ours) and washer W1 (cowl leads); grounds F7 / R2 / R3 to EB, F8 to EA. Rule R61: these stay fed from J/B No.1. Wiper / washer spots (Dan 2026-10-13, Route 2 rev 11, DECISIONS S19): F9 under the windshield cowl, driver side - its leads leave the left-kick landings through the driver (LH) fender pass-through (bp_l_pass) and run up to the cowl; W1 at the passenger front corner, lower front fender, on a drop from the RH corner branch.",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3210,
        "y": 240
      },
      "color": "Green"
    },
    {
      "id": "shdr_0",
      "text": "TRUNK + GLOVE BOX",
      "width": 270,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3210,
        "y": 1320
      },
      "color": "Green"
    },
    {
      "id": "shdr_2",
      "text": "CABIN LANDINGS (cowl side - J/B1, IE1, old R/B2 / R/B4 outputs, blower)",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3210,
        "y": 1680
      },
      "color": "Red"
    },
    {
      "id": "shdr_3",
      "text": "NEW ENGINE-ROOM LOADS - MR-S EHPS pump (one device: relay + 3 connectors) and both uprated fans",
      "width": 270,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3210,
        "y": 1800
      },
      "color": "Blue"
    },
    {
      "id": "note_acamp",
      "text": "A/C IS THE AMPLIFIERS' BUSINESS, NOT THE ECU'S OR THE CSB3'S - and there are TWO\nRead off the factory EWD automatic-A/C pages, saved in ewd-snips:\n  p150  AUTO A/C AMPLIFIER  A32=conn A, A33=conn B, A34=conn C\n        A1 Ambient Temp -> TAM, conn C pin 6, Y-B (via EA1 4, IQ1 1)\n        A27 Water Temp  -> TW,  conn C pin 20, R-G\n  p152  A/C AMPLIFIER A18 - a SEPARATE module\n        A5 Pressure SW  -> A18 pin 13, Y-R (via EB2 2, E10, IJ1 15)\nAmbient sensor -> amplifier stays FACTORY wiring (TAM not this pass, 2026-09-30).\nPressure switch A5-4 Y-R and clutch A4-3 Y-B land on ST185-ACAmp-Spur\nas flying leads at A/C AMPLIFIER A18 (pins 13 and 5); this loom does\nnot redraw them. New here: only the ACPS +12V feed, a flying lead into\nA5 pin 1 (V-R). The amplifier's own coolant switch comes from Engine-A\nvia bulkhead A c37/c38 and IX_AC_CTS (ST185-ACAmp-Spur). The ECU's only\nA/C tie is Aux 4 ACT kill, broken off from ST185-A-cabin onto\nST185-ACAmp-Spur as A18-11. Labels: docs/harness/ACAMP-SPUR-LABELS.md.",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3210,
        "y": 1950
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_cavity_notes",
      "text": "CAVITY NOTES - full text of the signals marked * on this drawing\nCondenser fan relay (uprated, diode) 85: ACTIVE-LOW Coil - Ign 5 / B13, diode-suppressed relay fitted (TE 7-1904094-9)\nMR-S EHPS pump (A power / B si A-1: [A 90980-12068 pin 1] +12V from k_eps 87 (glove box, ST185-CabinPower), passenger fender; 8 AWG (sized 2026-09-28 against the AMI-60 - sot/channels.csv k_eps c1)\nMR-S EHPS pump (A power / B si A-2: [A 90980-12068 pin 2] GND, 8 AWG to engine block / EB\nMR-S EHPS pump (A power / B si B-2: [B 90980-10897 pin 2] SPD Out - speed-pulse output to ECU-A A27\nMR-S EHPS pump (A power / B si C-1: [C 90980-10942 pin 1] IG-switched, MTA-2 MRS 7.5A - pump enable\nA/C Ambient Temp Sensor (EWD A 1: Ambient temp signal -> A/C amplifier. Thermistor, 2-wire. NOT an ECU input - the ECU has no use for outside air temp.\nA/C Ambient Temp Sensor (EWD A 2: Ambient temp sensor return -> A/C amplifier. The amp supplies its own sensor ground; do NOT tie this to chassis or to Gnd Out.\namb_temp (label): A/C Ambient Temp Sensor (EWD A1, behind front bumper)\nA/C Pressure Switch (EWD A5) - 1: +12V in, wire V-R. EWD p152. Fed from the glove-box MTA-3 ACPS, 10 A.\nA/C Pressure Switch (EWD A5) - 4: Switched out -> A/C AMPLIFIER A18 pin 13, wire Y-R. EWD p152.\nAUTO A/C AMPLIFIER A34 = conn  C-6: TAM - ambient temp in. EWD p150: A1 pin 2 -> EA1 4 -> IQ1 1 -> TAM, conn C pin 6, wire Y-B.\nA/C AMPLIFIER A18 (separate mo 13: A/C pressure switch in. EWD p152: A5 pin 4 -> EB2 2 -> E10 -> IJ1 15 -> A18 pin 13, wire Y-R. Shares this net with the A3 A/C idle-up VSV.",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3210,
        "y": 2640
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_jb_disposition",
      "text": "J/B AND RELAY BLOCK DISPOSITION - owned by docs/electrical/ENGINE-ROOM-POWER-REDISTRIBUTION.md (what is removed, where each ex-J/B2 / R/B load lands, glove-box fuse schedule). Read it there - this drawing does not repeat it.",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3210,
        "y": 4170
      },
      "color": "Red"
    },
    {
      "id": "n_rtr_gauge",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 4890,
        "y": 0
      },
      "text": "RETRACT MOTOR WIRE SIZE: the R2 / R3 leads are 16 AWG (motor) / 18 AWG (limit) like the factory leads they continue; the RTR fuse upstream of the OEM retract control relay R8 is 30 A (LMI L3). Question J1 in docs/OPEN-ITEMS.md."
    }
  ],
